### Send IPC messages from renderer to main process using ipcRenderer and ipcMain

Source: https://github.com/electron/electron/blob/main/docs/tutorial/tutorial-3-preload.md

Exposes an IPC invoke wrapper in preload.js, listens for the channel in main.js using ipcMain.handle before creating the window, and invokes the exposed ping method from renderer.js. Wrap ipcRenderer.invoke calls instead of exposing the entire ipcRenderer module directly to prevent arbitrary IPC attacks.

```javascript
const { contextBridge, ipcRenderer } = require('electron')

contextBridge.exposeInMainWorld('versions', {
  node: () => process.versions.node,
  chrome: () => process.versions.chrome,
  electron: () => process.versions.electron,
  ping: () => ipcRenderer.invoke('ping')
  // we can also expose variables, not just functions
})
```

```javascript
const { app, BrowserWindow, ipcMain } = require('electron/main')

const path = require('node:path')

const createWindow = () => {
  const win = new BrowserWindow({
    width: 800,
    height: 600,
    webPreferences: {
      preload: path.join(__dirname, 'preload.js')
    }
  })
  win.loadFile('index.html')
}
app.whenReady().then(() => {
  ipcMain.handle('ping', () => 'pong')
  createWindow()
})
```

```javascript
const func = async () => {
  const response = await window.versions.ping()
  console.log(response) // prints out 'pong'
}

func()
```

